    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project). Build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `contactPreference` = `'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`, following the existing pattern for derived read-only owner fields (like `locality`, `membershipNumber`).\n\nTwo hand-edited files:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema. This is the source of truth for the build-generated `OwnerDto`, so the field appears in the response DTO automatically.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(contactPreference(owner))\")` plus a small single-responsibility helper:\n   ```java\n   default String contactPreference(Owner owner) {\n       String email = owner.getEmail();\n       return email != null && !email.isBlank() ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nBecause the logic lives in the mapper, every owner responder (`GET`, create, update, list) picks it up with no duplication \u2014 no changes needed to the `Owner` entity, the OfficeFloor YAML, or the response functions. Both new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass.",
